    "body": "## Line and headline (D21, docs/labs/session-goal.md)\n\nLine: bench maintenance · not a research line (no count) · headline unchanged → unchanged\n\n## What and why\n\n`tests::the_transformer_control_is_parameter_matched_to_the_geometric_arm` in `crates/uor-r4-training/examples/mqar-bench.rs` first compiled after #2224 and failed at its tolerance assert. I looked for a merged change to the geometric stack's parameter count and found none:\n\n- `git log -S parameter_count -- crates/uor-r4-training/src/geometric_stack.rs` finds two commits. a5f8313 (#2174) introduced this test and froze 1,370,008. ca5bdc6 (#2193) added quaternion-valued maps, which are opt-in (`quaternion_weights=none` by default) and do not change the default shapes.\n- `StackConfig::shapes()` has not changed since #2174. I summed it by hand for `rrarra`, width 128, 4 heads, MLP 384, context 512, vocab 512, L2 read with rotation: **1,370,008**, so the frozen count is still correct.\n\nThe real cause is the tolerance. The test allowed a residual of `3 * width` = 384. But one hidden unit of the control MLP costs `3 * width * layers` = 2,304 parameters, so rounding to the nearest width can leave up to 1,152. The solved control has `mlp_hidden` 395 and 1,370,496 parameters, which is +488 over the arm and fails the old bound. The test has carried this since it was written; it went unnoticed because the test target did not compile.\n\n**Change:** the bound is now half a unit (`3 * width * layers / 2`). The control's solved width (395) and count (1,370,496) are frozen. The doc comment is corrected. There is also a short entry in `current-state.md`.\n\n**Proposal for the owner (not done here):** the [3 October direction](https://github.com/UOR-Foundation/uor-r4/issues/820#issuecomment-5971681179) says no transformer baselines. On that basis the `arm=transformer` control and this test could be retired. I kept them because they reproduce earlier recorded control results, and removing them is the owner's call.\n\n## Result\n\nTest-only fix; no model change. Decision: KEEP the frozen geometric count.\n\n## Checklist\n\n- [ ] Checks run at this exact head: **not yet.** The test must run on a GPU pod through `scripts/pod/uor-pod`. This cloud session has no Runpod credentials, and I did not compile anywhere. Proposed command on a pod: `cargo test -p uor-r4-training --example mqar-bench the_transformer_control_is_parameter_matched_to_the_geometric_arm`\n- [x] `rustfmt --check` on the changed file passes\n- [x] Research record: this is bench maintenance, so it is recorded in current-state only and has no lab README\n- [x] New entry at the top of `docs/integration/current-state.md`, with **Next:**\n- [x] STATUS.md / ROADMAP.md / #2028 table: state unchanged\n- [x] README: nothing a reader relies on changed\n- [x] `python3 scripts/check_claim_wording.py` passes\n\nReferences #2032\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/session_013aLwtD4wKqGQUmNXMGtNDG\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code/session_013aLwtD4wKqGQUmNXMGtNDG)_",
